---
/**
 * SpecimenReading - the doc, reading and detail family, printed live.
 *
 * ─── WHY THIS STAGE IS NOT AN ISLAND ──────────────────────────────────────
 * Almost nothing in this family ships JavaScript. A rail is an `<aside>` with a
 * grid, a contents register is an `<ol>`, a card is an anchor, an article is a
 * page's paper, an appendix is a badge strip or a tile grid, a foot is a rule
 * with two registers. The two exceptions are the family's own and are mounted
 * by the pages that need them: `Contents.ts` (the marking, one observer per
 * page) and `RustViewer`'s tab bar (the switch, now scoped to its own root).
 * The sheet mounts the second three times, which is exactly why the viewer's
 * script had to stop addressing the whole document.
 *
 * ─── THE RENDERER DECIDES NOTHING ────────────────────────────────────────
 * A row states what it is, which part it exercises, when that state is right and
 * the arm it prints; this file builds the data and mounts the block. That split
 * is why the matrix and the rows cannot drift: both read
 * `Content/Specimen/Reading.ts`, and a state added there appears on both with no
 * second edit.
 *
 * ─── THE DATA IS THE SITE'S OWN ──────────────────────────────────────────
 * Every section, route, count and sentence below is the kind of thing this
 * document states: a page of the manual, a clause of the licence, a crate of the
 * workspace, a part of the record. A specimen printed with lorem ipsum would
 * prove that the block can hold text; a specimen printed with the document's own
 * facts proves that the block can hold THIS document.
 *
 * ─── THE STAGE IS A PLATE, NOT A VIEWPORT ────────────────────────────────
 * The documentation shell pins its rail to `100dvh` and hides it below 1024px -
 * both are page behaviours, and a plate that simulated them would be printing a
 * browser. `_Reading.scss` therefore sets the rail static and bounded inside
 * `.specimen-reading__stage`, and says so where it does it: the sheet shows the
 * composition, and the composition is what the matrix is about.
 */
import {
	Groups,
	InGroup,
	type Specimen,
} from "../../Content/Specimen/Reading.js";

